[49.13868, "o", "> "]
[49.13875, "o", "You are provided with a biomedical multiple-choice QA dataset in the /app/data directory containing:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[49.13877, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[49.138799, "o", "- train.json: 300 training samples\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[49.138835, "o", "- val.json: 100 validation samples\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[49.138857, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[49.138943, "o", "NOTE: The test set is NOT available in the data folder during training to prevent overfitting. \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[49.13901, "o", "It is stored separately and only accessible during the evaluation phase.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[49.139045, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[49.139081, "o", "Each sample has the following structure:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[49.139106, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> {\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[49.139155, "o", "  \"question\": \"What is the primary function of hemoglobin?\",\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[49.139177, "o", "> "]
[49.139317, "o", "  \"options\": [\"A) Transport oxygen\", \"B) Fight infections\", \"C) Clot blood\", \"D) Digest food\"],  // Exactly 4 options (A, B, C, D)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   \"answer\": \"A\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[49.139372, "o", "}\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Requirements:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[49.139433, "o", "1. Use the openai-community/gpt2 model as the base model for fine-tuning\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[49.139495, "o", "2. Implement LoRA fine-tuning with the following configuration:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[49.139543, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>    - LoRA rank (r): 8\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[49.139568, "o", "   - LoRA alpha: 16\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[49.139611, "o", "   - Target modules: ['\"'\"'c_attn'\"'\"'] (attention layers)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[49.139653, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[49.139688, "o", "3. Train the model using the provided training and validation sets\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[49.139696, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[49.139783, "o", "4. Save your training script to /app/train_lora.py for verification\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[49.139813, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[49.139879, "o", "5. Save the trained LoRA adapter to /app/experiments/lora_adapter, including:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[49.139886, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[49.13993, "o", "   - adapter_config.json (LoRA configuration)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[49.139949, "o", "> "]
[49.13999, "o", "   - adapter_model.safetensors (LoRA weights)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[49.140042, "o", "   - tokenizer_config.json (tokenizer configuration)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[49.140146, "o", "   - adapter_config should include default arguments including '\"'\"'base_model_name_or_path'\"'\"' and '\"'\"'task_type'\"'\"' \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[49.140165, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[49.140233, "o", "6. It is recommended to use the PEFT (peft==0.15.0) library for implementing LoRA fine-tuning.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[49.140245, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[49.14031, "o", "7. Create a results file at /app/lora_results.json with the exact schema below\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
